                "topic": "Section I: Part B (Calculator Active)",
                "difficulty": "hard",
                "question": "<p>A stream flows into a lake at a rate of <img src=\"images/ed784edcc29b474ba7ed0f8196c56bff.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\">\r                             gallons per hour. A pump is used to remove water from the lake at a rate of 500 gallons per hour. At the beginning of a certain day, the lake contains 30,000 gallons of water. How much water is in the lake after 24 hours?</p>",
                "options": [
                    "11,520",
                    "29,520",
                    "41,020",
                    "41,520"
                ],
                "answer": "B",
                "explanation": "<strong>B</strong>  <p>The amount of water that\r                                 flows into the lake is calculated as:</p> <p><img src=\"images/d0c5dd19445a4c93b215c48b3132aa71.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"></p> <p>Use your calculator to\r                                 evaluate the integral: Enter the equation for <em>R</em> into Y= and adjust the viewing window as needed.\r                                 Press CALC (2<sup>nd</sup> TRACE) 7 (for the\r                                 <img src=\"images/69e6f4926b1b478bb922e0c930534e83.png\" class=\"exam-img\" style=\"max-width:100%; vertical-align:middle; margin:4px 0;\"> option). You’ll also need to enter the limits of\r                                 integration (here, the lower limit is 0 and the upper limit is 24).\r                                 The result is 11,520, but be careful—don’t pick (A), because you’re\r                                 not done yet. The amount of water pumped out of the lake over the\r                                 24-hour period is (500)(24) = 12,000\r                                 gallons. Thus, the amount of the water in the lake after\r                                 24 hours is computed as 30,000 + 11,520\r                                 − 12,000 = 29,520 gallons, which is (B).</p>"
